<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petrozavodsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petrozavodsk is a city on the western shore of Lake Onega and the capital of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It grew from an ironworks founded in 1703 on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> to make <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a>. It was capital of the Karelo-Finnish SSR from 1940 to 1956, and Finnish forces occupied it during the Continuation War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petrozavodsk.jpg" alt="Petrozavodsk" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Semenov.m7 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petrozavodsk_Collage_2020.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
